  "finalText": "Writing the deployment records now. `UnlessRetainer` is deployed on Arc testnet from the source that passed P4, and the on-chain code matches the local build once the USDC constructor argument is accounted for.\n\n- **Address:** `0x54414913081adb0d95b0f5aedc6a4c8a8d85c821`\n- **Deployment tx:** `0x5a421959e9218941d67139ca7e3caff8fa9d2d8b41d95f581b26699143ca8c7e`\n- **Block:** 69,092,835\n- **Explorer:** https://explorer.testnet.arc.io/address/0x54414913081adb0d95b0f5aedc6a4c8a8d85c821\n\n**Read-back from the deployed contract:**\n- `USDC()` returns `0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000`.\n- `nextRetainerId()` returns `0`.\n\n**Bytecode comparison:**\n\n| Hash | Value |\n|---|---|\n| On-chain runtime code (`cast code`, then keccak) | `0x392029f2c9e51b363392c3f23e99539f29cc86d4932c470635d07c8dc37a4d79` |\n| Local artifact `deployedBytecode`, raw | `0xb55307cd6fa12a300dc06259387577842a97685d3c6eeecf311d93fb17513ea7` |\n| Local artifact with the USDC address patched in | `0x392029f2c9e51b363392c3f23e99539f29cc86d4932c470635d07c8dc37a4d79` |\n\nThe raw local hash does not match the on-chain hash, and it was never going to. The artifact's `deployedBytecode` leaves the six `USDC` immutable slots as zeros, while the deployed code has the address filled in. After I patch the constructor argument into those six slots, the hash equals the on-chain one exactly (22,994 bytes each).\n\n**Mainnet comparison:** for the testnet-versus-mainnet check in runbook §6, compare on-chain code to on-chain code, which is what that section describes. Comparing a fresh local artifact would hit this same difference. I recorded all three hashes in the JSON with a note.\n\n**Files**\n- **`contracts/script/Deploy.s.sol`:** runbook §5.1 verbatim, with only the import changed to `\"../UnlessRetainer.sol\"`. It compiles. I deployed with Arc Studio's deploy tool, not by running this script, so the script is unused for now.\n- **`deployments/arc-testnet.json`:** the §3 shape plus the fields you asked for:\n  - `block`, `studioProjectUrl` and `openzeppelin` (`5.6.1`).\n  - `compiler`: solc 0.8.28, optimizer on with 200 runs, `cancun`, no `viaIR`.\n  - `deployer`, `runtimeBytecodeKeccak` and `localRuntimeBytecodeKeccak`.\n- **Extras I added:** `evidence/studio/p5-testnet-deploy.json` holds the deployment output. I also added the address to `AGENTS.md` and updated the status line in `README.md`.\n\n**`deployer` field:** it is `0x5B12Ce46C7194aD57d143bC22847224047b1Ef42`, Arc Studio's platform deployer wallet. The transaction itself was submitted by a bundler address, `0xf4b4…a066`. The wallet is a smart account, so a deploy appears as a user operation. The contract has no owner, so this address has no special rights.\n\nI did not change `contracts/UnlessRetainer.sol`, `foundry.toml`, `remappings.txt`, `package.json` or your two uploaded docs, and I wrote no mainnet configuration. The contract is now frozen: any change to those files means a redeploy.",
